<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gresik</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gresik is a port town on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, just north-west of Surabaya. From the fourteenth century it was a busy harbour for Chinese, Gujarati and Javanese traders and an early centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>: Maulana Malik Ibrahim was buried there in 1419, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunan-giri">Sunan Giri</a> founded his religious school on the hills nearby. It is now an industrial city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gresik.jpg" alt="Gresik" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Everyone Sinks Starco · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petrokimia_Gresik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
